msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-update.md:68
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-update.md:70
msgid ""
"This command updates the inputs in a lock file (`flake.lock`). **By default, "
"all inputs are updated**. If the lock file doesn't exist yet, it will be "
"created. If inputs are not in the lock file yet, they will be added."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-update.md:74
msgid ""
"Unlike other `nix flake` commands, `nix flake update` takes a list of names "
"of inputs to update as its positional arguments and operates on the flake in "
"the current directory. You can pass a different flake-url with `--flake` to "
"override that default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-update.md:78
msgid ""
"The related command [`nix flake lock`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-"
"lock.md) also creates lock files and adds missing inputs, but is safer as it "
"will never update inputs already in the lock file."
msgstr ""

